  "lapsed_date": "07/06/2009",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the additional floor and front walls hereby permitted, shall match those used in the existing building (white render finish) and the railings on the parapet roof and boundary wall shall be tubular powder coated metal.",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the flats are occupied.",
    "Condition : 4 - The proposed second floor window on the west flank shall be obscure glazed, hinged to open inwards and shall not be repaired or replaced otherwise than with obscured glazing.",
    "Condition : 5 - No additional flank windows or other glazed openings shall be formed in any wall of the additional floor hereby approved without the prior written consent of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 6 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 08.00 to 18.00 on Mondays to Fridays, and none on Saturdays, Sundays and public holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 7 - No development shall take place until full details of both hard and soft landscape works have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority and these works shall be carried out as approved.  These details shall include retention of the exsiting private amenity areas and hardstanding access to the rear of flats 1 and 2; means of enclosure; car parking layouts; other vehicle and pedestrian access and circulation areas; hard surfacing material; and details and position of refuse storage. Soft landscape works shall include planting plans and written specificationss of plants, noting species, plant sizes and proposed numbers/densities where appropriate.",
    "Condition : 8 - Prior to the commencement of any work on site, details shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority showing the height of the proposed front wall reduced to the same height as the sill of the existing ground floor windows, and the development shall be implemented as approved.",
    "Condition : 9 - Prior to the commencement of any work on site, details shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority in relation to an automatic gate mechanism if proposed.  Such details shall be implemented as approved.",
    "Condition : 10 - Before commencement of operations, a scheme shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority to cover the following matters:\r\n\r\n(i)\tany external illumination of the site relating to the construction period\r\n\r\n(ii)\tmeasures to ensure that all mud and other loose materials are not carried on the wheels and chassis of any vehicles leaving the site; and\r\n\r\n(iii)\tmeasures to minimise dust nuisance caused by the operations and to ensure that no dust or other debris is carried on to the adjoining properties.\r\n\r\nThe scheme so approved should be fully implemented.\r\n",
    "Condition : 11 - ."
  ],
